ail with query might do full-text. I could search for recent keywords. But better: the aggregate already says the newest is Sep 26. Something''s off — perhaps there are a lot of emails and sorting is weird.\n\nLet me try searchMail with queries to find anything this week. Maybe search by date isn''t supported. I could try searchMail with query \"November\" or \"Nov 2026\".\n\nAlso \"this week\" could have events/deadlines. Let me consider searching for emails mentioning deadlines. But first, gather more data: searchMail for recent, and listCalendars for events this week (Nov 2-8) to see what needs attention.\n\nLet me do: searchMail(mailboxId=null, query=\"2026\") — probably too broad. Alternatively search \"Nov\". Hmm.\n\nLet me search for tools: \"calendar events list\", and also do searchMail queries.\n\nI''ll run: searchMail \"week\" ... not useful.\n\nPlan: call search_tools for calendar events listing and member events. And searchMail with a couple of targeted queries like \"deadline\", \"invoice\", \"action required\", \"urgent\".\n\nActually a better approach: since aggregate inbox shows newest Sep 26, the mailbox likely genuinely has nothing newer... but that''s implausible for \"what needs attention this week.\" Let me check other folders (inbox only covers inbox). Perhaps archived/starred contain recent. Let me search mail generally.\n\nI''ll issue: searchMail query \"deadline OR urgent\" won''t work. Try query \"invitation\" and \"invoice\"? That returns old ones too.\n\nLet me try a date-ish query \"Nov 2026\".\n\nLet me do parallel: search_tools(\"list calendar events in range\"), search_tools(\"search email body thread folder\"), searchMail(overdue invoice).\n\nActually simpler: searchMail with query \"2026\" might match dates in body. Let''s just try a few.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The aggregate inbox''s most recent email is from Sep 26, 2026, but the turn is Nov 6, 2026. That''s odd — the inbox seems stale? Hmm, maybe the mailbox''s newest items are September. That''s a 6-week gap. Possibly the data is just seeded that way. But \"this week\" = week of Nov 6, 2026 (Mon Nov 2 – Sun Nov 8). No emails this week apparently.\n\nWait, maybe aggregateInbox returned sorted by date descending but only the top 15 and those are Sep. So the newest mail is Sep 26. That''s a big gap. Maybe there''s more mail in other folders or the mailbox is quiet. Let me search mail for recent items to check — maybe searchMail can filter by date? The query is a string. Let me try searching \"2026\" or something. Hmm.\n\nActually I should verify: searchMail with query might do full-text. I could search for recent keywords. But better: the aggregate already says the newest is Sep 26. Something''s off — perhaps there are a lot of emails and sorting is weird.\n\nLet me try searchMail with queries to find anything this week. Maybe search by date isn''t supported. I could try searchMail with query \"November\" or \"Nov 2026\".\n\nAlso \"this week\" could have events/deadlines. Let me consider searching for emails mentioning deadlines. But first, gather more data: searchMail for recent, and listCalendars for events this week (Nov 2-8) to see what needs attention.\n\nLet me do: searchMail(mailboxId=null, query=\"2026\") — probably too broad. Alternatively search \"Nov\". Hmm.\n\nLet me search for tools: \"calendar events list\", and also do searchMail queries.\n\nI''ll run: searchMail \"week\" ... not useful.\n\nPlan: call search_tools for calendar events listing and member events. And searchMail with a couple of targeted queries like \"deadline\", \"invoice\", \"action required\", \"urgent\".\n\nActually a better approach: since aggregate inbox shows newest Sep 26, the mailbox likely genuinely has nothing newer... but that''s implausible for \"what needs attention this week.\" Let me check other folders (inbox only covers inbox). Perhaps archived/starred contain recent. Let me search mail generally.\n\nI''ll issue: searchMail query \"deadline OR urgent\" won''t work. Try query \"invitation\" and \"invoice\"? That returns old ones too.\n\nLet me try a date-ish query \"Nov 2026\".\n\nLet me do parallel: search_tools(\"list calendar events in range\"), search_tools(\"search email body thread folder\"), searchMail(overdue invoice).\n\nActually simpler: searchMail with query \"2026\" might match dates in body. Let''s just try a few."}],"createdAt":1795579755529},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"results":[{"name":"listEvents","description":"List calendar events between two ISO-8601 timestamps across every visible calendar in the workspace, merged and sorted by start time. Narrow with c...","score":12.91},{"name":"findMemberEvents","description":"List calendar events in a time window that one workspace member organises or is invited to, across every visible calendar in the workspace. Use to ...","score":12.2},{"name":"updateEvent","description":"Change fields on an existing calendar event. Only the fields you pass are modified.","score":4.94},{"name":"listReadLater","description":"List the email ids on your read-later list in a specific mailbox, newest first. Fetch each with getEmail.","score":4.76},{"name":"listMuted","description":"List the threadIds of the conversations you muted in a specific mailbox.","score":4.51}],"loaded":["listEvents","findMemberEvents","updateEvent","listReadLater","listMuted"],"message":"Found and loaded 5 tool(s): listEvents, findMemberEvents, updateEvent, listReadLater, listMuted. They are available on your next turn — call them directly."},"toolCallId":"call_resp_01a210e4-a3ea-7f32-bdd5-baaaf8dcad08_0","toolName":"search_tools","args":{"query":"list calendar events in a date range"}},"updatedAt":1795579755941},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"results":[{"name":"listEmails","description":"List emails from a folder in ONE specific connected mailbox. Pass the returned nextPageToken back as pageToken to fetch the next page.","score":13.56},{"name":"getThread","description":"Fetch every email in a conversation thread in a specific mailbox, oldest first. Use the threadId returned by listEmails, aggregateInbox, or searchM...","score":11.21},{"name":"listReadLater","description":"List the email ids on your read-later list in a specific mailbox, newest first. Fetch each with getEmail.","score":10.75},{"name":"deleteEmails","description":"Move the listed emails to the trash in a specific mailbox. Provide the mailboxId and the exact email ids.","score":9.85},{"name":"getEmail","description":"Fetch the full plain-text body of an email in a specific mailbox. Provide the mailboxId it belongs to.","score":9.22}],"loaded":["listEmails","getThread","listReadLater","deleteEmails","getEmail"],"message":"Found and loaded 5 tool(s): listEmails, getThread, listReadLater, deleteEmails, getEmail. They are available on your next turn — call them directly. Some were already loaded."},"toolCallId":"call_resp_01a210e4-a3ea-7f32-bdd5-baaaf8dcad08_1","toolName":"search_tools","args":{"query":"read email body and thread, list emails in a folder"}},"updatedAt":1795579755942},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":0,"emails":[]},"toolCallId":"call_resp_01a210e4-a3ea-7f32-bdd5-baaaf8dcad08_2","toolName":"searchMail","args":{"mailboxId":null,"query":"November 2026"}},"updatedAt":1795579755942},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1795579755945,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/metis/demo"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Search for \"November 2026\" returned nothing. Let me check other folders — maybe newer mail is in archive/starred? Actually aggregate inbox covers inbox; newest Sep 26. That suggests inbox stops there.\n\nWait — maybe listEmails inbox returns newest first, and aggregate is same. Let me check folder \"starred\" and \"archive\" for recent, plus listCalendars and listEvents for this week (Nov 2–8, 2026).\n\nAlso maybe searchMail for \"deadline