a threads with actions outstanding — e.g., Priya''s Arabic proofs, Kenji''s Japanese email (新ブランド案のご確認について = \"about confirming the new brand proposal\") which is a request in Japanese that may not have been answered. Let''s check the sent folder to see if replies were made. Hmm, that''s a lot of work. Given \"what needs my attention this week,\" a good answer: no new mail this week; here''s what''s still open and what''s coming up.\n\nLet me gather: starred folder list, read-later list, and getEmail for the Northbeam booking confirmation and schedule change, and Kenji''s Japanese email.\n\nActually keep it efficient. Let me do:\n- listEmails starred\n- listReadLater\n- getEmail Northbeam booking confirmed (id WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM4NF0)\n- getEmail Northbeam schedule change (WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDQwMl0)\n- getEmail Kenji Japanese (WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM5M10)\n\nAlso check sent folder to see if there''s a reply to Kenji. Let me do that too: listEmails sent limit 20.\n\nWait — but the flight is Nov 9 which is next Monday, outside \"this week\" but still imminent. The user asks about mailboxes, so mail focus.\n\nLet me run these calls.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The inbox''s newest email is Sep 26, 2026 — over 6 weeks ago. So there''s no mail \"this week.\" The calendar has lots of noise (Bulk calendar with fake events, Edge cases). Real work events: Daily standup (recurring), Weekly 1:1 Ana/Raj, Monthly studio review.\n\nThe listEvents was capped at 104 (max 250? count 104 — hmm, that''s the actual returned count; it may have truncated). Notably the real Work calendar events appear only Nov 2-3, then nothing after Nov 6? Actually Work events: Nov 2 monthly review, Nov 3 1:1, daily standups Nov 2-6, Nov 5, Nov 6. After Nov 6 09:00 nothing in Work. But the \"max\" default may have truncated results at 104; the results seem sorted and end at Nov 8 23:45, so full window covered likely.\n\nWait — important: the bulk calendar events look like seeded noise. The us