r.\n2. Kenji/Japanese reply — overdue 11 weeks; but now less urgent since Oct 8 review passed.\n3. Travel NB7Q4K — has already happened (Mon 9 Nov); deprioritized, only the budget note to Sam remains unsent.\n4. Priya Arabic/English — open but no date.\n\nAnswer concisely, and note the clock: today is Wed 25 Nov 2026 04:10 UTC (this message''s clock), not 6 Nov — so my earlier framing shifts. That''s important to state: \"since you asked, the calendar moved: today is 25 Nov.\"\n\nAlso mention the mailbox still hasn''t received anything since 26 Sep — that''s odd but that''s what''s there, and it means the venue thread has been silent for 11 weeks.\n\nI should note the launch isn''t on any calendar (Work/Personal have only standups and 1:1s through 1 Dec), so no booking/event exists for 26 Nov — supporting the \"unconfirmed\" point.\n\nKeep it tight.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"State is unchanged: nothing has arrived since 26 Sep; nothing sent since 18 Sep; the draft to Mira is still unsent. Now today is Wed 25 Nov 2026, 04:10 UTC. The Aozora launch at Harbour Hall is Thu 26 Nov — tomorrow. And there is no launch event on the calendar (no venue booking event, no launch event).\n\nSo the most urgent: the Harbour Hall terms/venue for tomorrow''s launch — the draft to Mira has never been sent, and there''s no reply from Mira since 9 Sep when she said she''d send terms (she never did, and Ana never chased). So the 26 Nov launch at Harbour Hall is unconfirmed by any written agreement, and it''s tomorrow.\n\nAlso note: Ana was in Tokyo Nov 9–? (flight arrived Nov 10). Possibly still traveling — unknown. Careful not to over-claim.\n\nSecond: the English menu version (Priya/Layla) — tied to the same launch? Possibly related to Saffron & Sage, not Aozora. Uncertain.\n\nRanking:\n1. Harbour Hall / 26 Nov launch — <36 hours, no terms, draft unsent, no venue event on calendar.\n2. Kenji/Japanese reply — overdue 11 weeks; but now less urgent since Oct 8 review passed.\n3. Travel NB7Q4K — has already happened (Mon 9 Nov); deprioritized, only the budget note to Sam remains unsent.\n4. Priya Arabic/English — open but no date.\n\nAnswer concisely, and note the clock: today is Wed 25 Nov 2026 04:10 UTC (this message''s clock), not 6 Nov — so my earlier framing shifts. That''s important to state: \"since you asked, the calendar moved: today is 25 Nov.\"\n\nAlso mention the mailbox still hasn''t received anything since 26 Sep — that''s odd but that''s what''s there, and it means the venue thread has been silent for 11 weeks.\n\nI should note the launch isn''t on any calendar (Work/Personal have only standups and 1:1s through 1 Dec), so no booking/event exists for 26 Nov — supporting the \"unconfirmed\" point.\n\nKeep it tight."}],"createdAt":1795579822243},{"type":"text","text":"**The Harbour Hall venue for tomorrow''s Aozora launch — that''s the one.**\n\nNote the clock has moved: your message is stamped **Wed 25 Nov 2026, 04:10 UTC**, not 6 Nov. Re-checking just now:\n\n- Inbox still has nothing newer than **Sat 26 Sep**, and you''ve sent nothing since **Fri 18 Sep**.\n- The \"Terms for November 26\" draft to mira@harbourhallvenues.com is **still unsent** — it never got past \"1.\".\n- Mira''s last word is still 9 Sep: the terrace room, 80 standing, plinths, **26 Nov held**, \"I''ll send terms this week.\" Those terms never arrived in the mailbox, and you never chased.\n- Your Work and Personal calendars for 24 Nov – 3 Dec contain only standups and the 1:1s. **There is no venue booking or launch event on 26 Nov anywhere on your calendars.**\n\nSo the launch is under 36 hours away with no signed terms, no deposit trail, and no calendar entry — and the one email that would resolve it has been sitting in drafts for nine weeks.\n\nRanked against the rest:\n\n1. **Harbour Hall / 26 Nov** — live, tomorrow, no paper. Send the terms email now, even if it''s just \"we''re on for tomorrow — confirm the hold and send the terms/contract.\"\n2. **Kenji Watanabe** — overdue 11 weeks, but the 8 Oct review it referenced has already passed; it''s a relationship repair, not a deadline.\n3. **Priya / Layla English menu version** — open, no date attached.\n4. **Northbeam NB7Q4K** — moot: that Lisbon→Tokyo flight departed Mon 9 Nov. Only loose end is the unsent budget note to Sam.\n\nWant me to finish the draft to Mira, or start a fresh, shorter one that just nails down tomorrow? And should I put the 26 Nov launch on your Work calendar?","createdAt":1795579822243}],"metadata":{"modelId":"metis/demo","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**The Harbour Hall venue for tomorrow''s Aozora launch — that''s the one.**\n\nNote the clock has moved: your message is stamped **Wed 25 Nov 2026, 04:10 UTC**, not 6 Nov. Re-checking just now:\n\n- Inbox still has nothing newer than **Sat 26 Sep**, and you''ve sent nothing since **Fri 18 Sep**.\n- The \"Terms for November 26\" draft to mira@harbourhallvenues.com is **still unsent** — it never got past \"1.\".\n- Mira''s last word is still 9 Sep: the terrace room, 80 standing, plinths, **26 Nov held**, \"I''ll send terms this week.\" Those terms never arrived in the mailbox, and you never chased.\n- Your Work and Personal calendars for 24 Nov – 3 Dec contain only standups and the 1:1s. **There is no venue booking or launch event on 26 Nov anywhere on your calendars.**\n\nSo the launch is under 36 hours away with no signed terms, no deposit trail, and no calendar entry — and the one email that would resolve it has been sitting in drafts for nine weeks.\n\nRanked against the rest:\n\n1. **Harbour Hall / 26 Nov** — live, tomorrow, no paper. Send the terms email now, even if it''s just \"we''re on for tomorrow — confirm the hold and send the terms/contract.\"\n2. **Kenji Watanabe** — overdue 11 weeks, but the 8 Oct review it referenced has already passed; it''s a relationship repair, not a deadline.\n3. **Priya / Layla English menu version** — open, no date attached.\n4. **Northbeam NB7Q4K** — moot: that Lisbon→Tokyo flight departed Mon 9 Nov. Only loose end is the unsent budget note to Sam.\n\nWant me to finish the draft to Mira, or start a fresh, shorter one that just nails down tomorrow? And should I put the 26 Nov launch on your Work calendar?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-25T04:10:14.001Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
