tail besides listEvents query. I could listEvents query \"Design review\" to get details — I already have the fields. No description field returned though.\n\nAlso note it''s 7 weeks in the past.\n\nKeep it tight and direct."}],"createdAt":1795579852313},{"type":"text","text":"**It isn''t on any calendar.** The only record of a \"Rebrand review\" is Raj''s email invitation in your inbox (24 Sep 2026):\n\n> Raj invited you to Rebrand review on **Thu 8 Oct 2026, 15:00–15:45 UTC**. Join: https://linkroom.app/r/rebrand-review\n\nNo event with that title exists on any of your four calendars (Work, Personal, Bulk, Edge cases) — so it was never accepted, or it was declined and removed. If it *had* been accepted it would sit on your **Work** calendar, since that''s the calendar your meeting invitations land on and where the rest of the Aozora series lives (logo review 1 Oct, kickoff 5 Oct, Kenji sync 9 Oct).\n\nOne near-miss you should know about: your **Work** calendar does have a **\"Design review\"** on **Thu 8 Oct 2026, 15:00–16:00 UTC, Studio 2** — same start time, but a different title, no attendees listed, and in a room rather than the Linkroom. It may be the rebrand review renamed, or it may be a separate meeting; the calendar data can''t tell me which, and there''s no description on it.\n\nEither way it''s seven weeks past — if you''re chasing what came out of that review, the answer is in the calendar''s \"Design review\" slot, not under a rebrand title.","createdAt":1795579852313}],"metadata":{"modelId":"metis/demo","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**It isn''t on any calendar.** The only record of a \"Rebrand review\" is Raj''s email invitation in your inbox (24 Sep 2026):\n\n> Raj invited you to Rebrand review on **Thu 8 Oct 2026, 15:00–15:45 UTC**. Join: https://linkroom.app/r/rebrand-review\n\nNo event with that title exists on any of your four calendars (Work, Personal, Bulk, Edge cases) — so it was never accepted, or it was declined and remove