er without \"order\". Eh — \"shipped\" search covered Swiftpost. Let me do getEmail A-42.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"No order-tracking tool exists — my scope is mail/calendar/drives. The most recent shipment: Brightloom order A-42 shipped Wed 23 Sep 2026, in ana@demo.trymetis.email inbox. That''s two months ago, not \"recently\". No Shopify/order system connected.\n\nWait — there was an Aug 1 Swiftpost parcel then Aug 4 delivered. Sep 18 order A-42, Sep 23 shipped. Nothing after 23 Sep. And nothing in other mailboxes? searchMail returned only ana@ mailbox. Are there other mailboxes? The results tag \"mailbox\" singular. Presumably multiple mailboxes exist but only this one has matches. I shouldn''t claim there are multiple mailboxes without checking. Earlier turns were about one mailbox. I''ll just say \"your mailbox ana@demo.trymetis.email\" — hmm, careful: searchMail searches every mailbox by default and results are tagged; all matches came from ana@demo.trymetis.email. That''s a fair statement.\n\nShould I read the A-42 email body for tracking details/delivery status? Yes — to answer whether it shipped and where it is. Let me get that email. Also check whether there''s a delivery confirmation for A-42 — no Swiftpost email after 23 Sep, so probably undelivered/no further updates. Let me read A-42 shipped email.\n\nI''ll call getEmail (need it loaded? Earlier I used getEmail in turn 1 — it''s loaded presumably). Yes, getEmail was used earlier. Let me call it.\n\nShould I also do aggregateInbox to see if anything recent mentions delivery? Maybe search \"delivered\". Actually search \"order\" covered. Let me just read the A-42 ship email, and search \"delivery\" quickly.\n\nActually keep it efficient: getEmail A-42 + search \"delivered\" maybe. I''ll do getEmail only plus a search for \"parcel\" to catch anything newer without \"order\". Eh — \"shipped\" search covered Swiftpost. Let me do getEmail A-42."}],"createdAt":1795579918738},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDQxMl0","truncated":false,"raw":"From: Brightloom <orders@brightloom.com>\r\nTo: Ana Silva <ana@demo.trymetis.email>\r\nSubject: Your order A-42 has shipped\r\nDate: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0000\r\nMessage-ID: <37h3c07pg079ehne@brightloom.com>\r\nMIME-Version: 1.0\r\nContent-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8\r\nContent-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\r\n\r\n<html>\r\n<head>\r\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">\r\n{\r\n  \"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"ParcelDelivery\",\r\n  \"carrier\": { \"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Swiftpost\" },\r\n  \"trackingNumber\": \"SP4471920385PT\",\r\n  \"trackingUrl\": \"https://swiftpost.com/track/SP4471920385PT\",\r\n  \"expectedArrivalUntil\": \"2026-09-30T20:00:00+00:00\",\r\n  \"partOfOrder\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Order\",\r\n    \"orderNumber\": \"A-42\",\r\n    \"merchant\": { \"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Brightloom\" }\r\n  },\r\n  \"itemShipped\": { \"@type\": \"Product\", \"name\": \"Walnut desk lamp\" }\r\n}\r\n</script>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n<p>Good news, your order A-42 is on its way.</p>\r\n<p>Walnut desk lamp, shipped with Swiftpost. Expected by September 30.</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://swiftpost.com/track/SP4471920385PT\">Track your package</a></p>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n"},"toolCallId":"call_resp_01a210e7-1d56-74d1-ae40-70bf04649751_0","toolName":"getRawEmail","args":{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDQxMl0","mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134"}},"updatedAt":1795579918743},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1795579918745,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/metis/demo"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Now, \"recently\" = relative to 25 Nov 2026. The last shipment was 23 Sep, expected by 30 Sep. No delivery confirmation for A-42 in the mailbox (the Swiftpost delivered emails are from Feb 2025, Apr 2026, Aug 2026). So: A-42 shipped 23 Sep with expected arrival by 30 Sep, but there''s no delivery email for it — worth flagging.\n\nAlso no order-shipped events after 23 Sep, so nothing shipped in the last two months.\n\nAnswer concisely: No, nothing recent. The last shipment was A-42 on 23 Sep — nearly nine weeks ago. Details: walnut desk lamp, Swiftpost SP4471920385PT, ETA 30 Sep. And no delivery confirmation for it — earlier orders (A-38 in Aug) got Swiftpost delivery emails on 4 Aug. So either the confirmation never came or went elsewhere.\n\nAlso note I have no order-system connector; this is from mail only.\n\nMath: 23 Sep to 25 Nov = 63 days, 9 weeks. Yes.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Now, \"recently\" = relative to 25 Nov 2026. The last shipment was 23 Sep, expected by 30 Sep. No delivery confirmation for A-42 in the mailbox (the Swiftpost delivered emails are from Feb 2025, Apr 2026, Aug 2026). So: A-42 shipped 23 Sep with expected arrival by 30 Sep, but there''s no delivery email for it — worth flagging.\n\nAlso no order-shipped events after 23 Sep, so nothing shipped in the last two months.\n\nAnswer concisely: No, nothing recent. The last shipment was A-42 on 23 Sep — nearly nine weeks ago. Details: walnut desk lamp, Swiftpost SP4471920385PT, ETA 30 Sep. And no delivery confirmation for it — earlier orders (A-38 in Aug) got Swiftpost delivery emails on 4 Aug. So either the confirmation never came or went elsewhere.\n\nAlso note I have no order-system connector; this is from mail only.\n\nMath: 23 Sep to 25 Nov = 63 days, 9 weeks. Yes."}],"createdAt":1795579924658},{"type":"text","text":"**Nothing recent — your last shipment was 23 September, nine weeks ago.** And I can only answer this from your mail, since no store or courier account is connected to this workspace.\n\nOne shipment is on record, in **ana@demo.trymetis.email**:\n\n- **Brightloom order A-42** — \"Your order A-42 has shipped\", Wed 23 Sep 2026 10:00 UTC. One **walnut desk lamp**, carried by **Swiftpost**, tracking **SP4471920385PT** (swiftpost.com/track/SP4471920385PT), expected arrival by **30 Sep 2026, 20:00 UTC**. The order itself was placed 18 Sep.\n\nThe thing worth flagging: **there''s no delivery confirmation for A-42.** Every earlier Brightloom order got a matching pair of Swiftpost emails — A-38 shipped 1 Aug and was \"out for delivery\" and \"delivered\" on 4 Aug; A-31 shipped 15 Apr, delivered 24 Apr. For A-42 you have the dispatch notice and nothing after it, despite the parcel being due two months ago. Possible explanations: a lost delivery notification, or the lamp genuinely never arrived. If it''s the latter you''re outside Brightloom''s usual window by a wide margin, so it''s worth checking the tracking link directly.\n\nNothing else has shipped since — no order, dispatch, parcel or tracking mail at all after 23 Sep.","createdAt":1795579924658}],"metadata":{"modelId":"metis/demo","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Nothing recent — your last shipment was 23 September, nine weeks ago.** And I can only answer this from your mail, since no store or courier account is connected to this workspace.\n\nOne shipment is on record, in **ana@demo.trymetis.email**:\n\n- **Brightloom order A-42** — \"Your order A-42 has shipped\", Wed 23 Sep 2026 10:00 UTC. One **walnut desk lamp**, carried by **Swiftpost**, tracking **SP4471920385PT** (swiftpost.com/track/SP4471920385PT), expected arrival by **30 Sep 2026, 20:00 UTC**. The order itself was placed 18 Sep.\n\nThe thing worth flagging: **there''s no delivery confirmation for A-42.** Every earlier Brightloom order got a matching pair of Swiftpost emails — A-38 shipped 1 Aug and was \"out for delivery\" and \"delivered\" on 4 Aug; A-31 shipped 15 Apr, delivered 24 Apr. For A-42 you have the dispatch notice and nothing after it, despite the parcel being due two months ago. Possible explanations: a lost delivery notification, or the lamp genuinely never arrived. If it''s the latter you''re outside Brightloom''s usual window by a wide ma