 2026).\n\nActually is Ledgerline a subscription she pays? \"Your Ledgerline invoice LL-2025xxx\" monthly — an expense. The absence of Oct/Nov invoices is a change worth flagging, since she may have cancelled it.\n\nAlso the Voltaro Energy \"Payment received\" 27 Mar 2026 — that''s a payment to her energy supplier presumably. Only two, Mar 2026 and Dec 2025 — not recent.\n\nAlso the phishing: spam has \"Konkan Bank: Action required: your account **4821 is suspended\" 15 Sep 2026 from konkan-bank-secure.com — lookalike. Real is konkanbank.in. Must flag. Also \"Overdue invoice #88213\" from ledgerl1ne-invoices.com — a lookalike of Ledgerline (ledgerline.io) using digit \"1\"! That''s a phishing attempt too, dated 9 Sep 2026. Good catch — \"ledgerl1ne-invoices.com\" with numeric one. Definitely flag as phishing.\n\nAlso note the 17 Apr debit INR 6,300 and 29 Apr credit INR 6,300 — that was the broken lamp purchase/refund probably. Already known; not \"lately\".\n\nSo the answer:\n\nHeadline: Very little — the last debit alert is 25 Sep, two months ago. INR 2,680 total over the past ~4 months visible in alerts, all small UPI spends.\n\nTable of recent debits:\n- 25 Sep 2026, INR 1,250, VPA chaiwala.store@konkan, UPI ref 427311009876, balance after 48,210.55\n- 12 Sep 2026, INR 450, chaiwala.store@konkan, 427310102947, balance 49,460.55\n- 2 Aug 2026, INR 2,760, tavola.mumbai@upi, 427310095028, balance 52,833.70\n- 8 Jun 2026, INR 980, metro.pune@upi, 427310087109, balance 60,072.40\n\nBalance trajectory: 60,072.40 (Jun) → 52,833.70 (Aug) → 49,460.55 (12 Sep) → 48,210.55 (25 Sep). Falling balance with no credits appearing in alerts. Hmm, careful: only debits searched. There were credit emails (29 Apr INR 6,300 credited). Let me not over-claim. Actually maybe I should search \"credited\" to see if income arrives. That would improve the picture. But the question was \"money moving out\" — I can note balances. It''s a fair caveat: no credit alerts since Apr, so I can''t tell what''s replenishing.\n\nAlso the arithmetic oddity: 12 Sep balance 49,460.55 minus 1,250 = 48,210.55 ✓ consistent. 2 Aug 52,833.70; 12 Sep balance 49,460.55 → 3,373.15 left between 2 Aug and 12 Sep unaccounted (only 450 debit on 12 Sep) → so ~2,923 of spending between 2 Aug and 12 Sep has no alert email. Similarly 8 Jun 60,072.40 → 2 Aug 52,833.70 = 7,238.70 gone, but only the 2,760 debit is documented. So alerts are incomplete — merchant alerts don''t cover everything (small UPI under threshold, or auto-debits). That''s a genuinely useful observation: the balance drops faster than the alerts account for, so email alerts are not a complete ledger.\n\nLet me verify the balance math carefully:\n- 8 Jun: after debit balance 60,072.40\n- 2 Aug: after debit 52,833.70 → difference 7,238.70; documented debit 2,760 → 4,478.70 unaccounted between 8 Jun and 2 Aug.\n- 12 Sep: after debit 49,460.55 → difference from 2 Aug: 3,373.15; documented 450 → 2,923.15 unaccounted.\n- 25 Sep: 48,210.55 = 49,460.55 − 1,250 ✓ exactly.\n\nSo between June and September about INR 7,400 left the account with no matching alert. And after 25 Sep there are no alerts at all for two months — either nothing spent (unlikely if grocery/UPI habits continue) or alerts stopped/being filtered.\n\nAlso: check spam for something? Also check whether there might be a filter. Can''t check filters.\n\nAlso should I search \"credited\" to check income? Quick and useful for the \"is balance falling\" claim. And search \"UPI\" maybe. Let me do one more parallel batch: \"credited\", \"UPI\". That''s reasonable before answering. Also maybe \"subscription\"/\"renewal\" — Ledgerline gap. Let me check the latest Ledgerline invoice amount? LL-2025111 — reading it would tell the monthly cost and whether it''s auto-charged. Worth one fetch. Let''s do: searchMail \"credited\", searchMail \"subscription\", getRawEmail 379 (LL-2025111).\n\nActually the Ledgerline invoices: if it''s a monthly subscription paid by card, the charge would appear as a bank debit — but no monthly INR debits appear in alerts, so maybe paid from another account/card. Reading the invoice reveals amount and payment method. Fine, one fetch.\n\nLet me do these three.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Only one mailbox. No banking tool. Now construct the answer.\n\n\"Lately\" — from 25 Nov 2026. Latest debit alert: 25 Sep 2026 (INR 1,250 to chaiwala.store@konkan via UPI). Then 12 Sep (450, same merchant). Then 2 Aug (2,760 tavola.mumbai@upi), 8 Jun (980 metro.pune@upi).\n\nAlso there''s a monthly Ledgerline subscription invoice — LL-2025111 on 1 Sep 2026, and no invoice on 1 Oct or 1 Nov 2026? Let''s check: invoices listed monthly: 1 Sep 2026 (LL-2025111), 1 Aug (110), 1 Jul, 1 Jun, 1 May, 1 Apr... and nothing after 1 Sep. That''s notable — the subscription invoices stopped after 1 Sep! That could suggest the subscription was cancelled, or billing moved. Interesting but that''s invoice issuance, not money out. Hmm, worth a note: Ledgerline invoices stop at LL-2025111 (1 Sep 2026).\n\nActually is Ledgerline a subscription she pays? \"Your Ledgerline invoice LL-2025xxx\" monthly — an expense. The absence of Oct/Nov invoices is a change worth flagging, since she may have cancelled it.\n\nAlso the Voltaro Energy \"Payment received\" 27 Mar 2026 — that''s a payment to her energy supplier presumably. Only two, Mar 2026 and Dec 2025 — not recent.\n\nAlso the phishing: spam has \"Konkan Bank: Action required: your account **4821 is suspended\" 15 Sep 2026 from konkan-bank-secure.com — lookalike. Real is konkanbank.in. Must flag. Also \"Overdue invoice #88213\" from ledgerl1ne-invoices.com — a lookalike of Ledgerline (ledgerline.io) using digit \"1\"! That''s a phishing attempt too, dated 9 Sep 2026. Good catch — \"ledgerl1ne-invoices.com\" with numeric one. Definitely flag as phishing.\n\nAlso note the 17 Apr debit INR 6,300 and 29 Apr credit INR 6,300 — that was the broken lamp purchase/refund probably. Already known; not \"lately\".\n\nSo the answer:\n\nHeadline: Very little — the last debit alert is 25 Sep, two months ago. INR 2,680 total over the past ~4 months visible in alerts, all small UPI spends.\n\nTable of recent debits:\n- 25 Sep 2026, INR 1,250, VPA chaiwala.store@konkan, UPI ref 427311009876, balance after 48,210.55\n- 12 Sep 2026, INR 450, chaiwala.store@konkan, 427310102947, balance 49,460.55\n- 2 Aug 2026, INR 2,760, tavola.mumbai@upi, 427310095028, balance 52,833.70\n- 8 Jun 2026, INR 980, metro.pune@upi, 427310087109, balance 60,072.40\n\nBalance trajectory: 60,072.40 (Jun) → 52,833.70 (Aug) → 49,460.55 (12 Sep) → 48,210.55 (25 Sep). Falling balance with no credits appearing in alerts. Hmm, careful: only debits searched. There were credit emails (29 Apr INR 6,300 credited). Let me not over-claim. Actually maybe I should search \"credited\" to see if income arrives. That would improve the picture. But the question was \"money moving out\" — I can note balances. It''s a fair caveat: no credit alerts since Apr, so I can''t tell what''s replenishing.\n\nAlso the arithmetic oddity: 12 Sep balance 49,460.55 minus 1,250 = 48,210.55 ✓ consistent. 2 Aug 52,833.70; 12 Sep balance 49,460.55 → 3,373.15 left between 2 Aug and 12 Sep unaccounted (only 450 debit on 12 Sep) → so ~2,923 of spending between 2 Aug and 12 Sep has no alert email. Similarly 8 Jun 60,072.40 → 2 Aug 52,833.70 = 7,238.70 gone, but only the 2,760 debit is documented. So alerts are incomplete — merchant alerts don''t cover everything (small UPI under threshold, or auto-debits). That''s a genuinely useful observation: the balance drops faster than the alerts account for, so email alerts are not a complete ledger.\n\nLet me verify the balance math carefully:\n- 8 Jun: after debit balance 60,072.40\n- 2 Aug: after debit 52,833.70 → difference 7,238.70; documented debit 2,760 → 4,478.70 unaccounted between 8 Jun and 2 Aug.\n- 12 Sep: after debit 49,460.55 → difference from 2 Aug: 3,373.15; documented 450 → 2,923.15 unaccounted.\n- 25 Sep: 48,210.55 = 49,460.55 − 1,250 ✓ exactly.\n\nSo between June and September about INR 7,400 left the account with no matching alert. And after 25 Sep there are no alerts at all for two months — either nothing spent (unlikely if grocery/UPI habits continue) or alerts stopped/being filtered.\n\nAlso: check spam for something? Also check whether there might be a filter. Can''t check filters.\n\nAlso should I search \"credited\" to check income? Quick and useful for the \"is balance falling\" claim. And search \"UPI\" maybe. Let me do one more parallel batch: \"credited\", \"UPI\". That''s reasonable before answering. Also maybe \"subscription\"/\"renewal\" — Ledgerline gap. Let me check the latest Ledgerline invoice amount? LL-2025111 — reading it would tell the monthly cost and whether it''s auto-charged. Worth one fetch. Let''s do: searchMail \"credited\", searchMail \"subscription\", getRawEmail 379 (LL-2025111).\n\nActually the Ledgerline invoices: if it''s a monthly subscription paid by card, the charge would appear as a bank debit — but no monthly INR debits appear in alerts, so maybe paid from another account/card. Reading the invoice reveals amount and payment method. Fine, one fetch.\n\nLet me do these three."}],"createdAt":1795579991052},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":1,"emails":[{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","mailbox":"ana@demo.trymetis.email","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDMyMV0","threadId":"<43dquw4gd2dpdh12@konkanbank.in>","from":"Konkan Bank","subject":"INR 6,300.00 credited to a/c **4821","date":"Wed Apr 29 2026 11:20:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""}]},"toolCallId":"call_resp_01a210e8-2453-7bb9-b9d6-0f3155027a20_0","toolName":"searchMail","args":{"mailboxId":null,"query":"credited"}},"updatedAt":1795579991450},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9