"},"toolCallId":"call_resp_01a210e8-2453-7bb9-b9d6-0f3155027a20_1","toolName":"getRawEmail","args":{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM3OV0","mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134"}},"updatedAt":1795579991450},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1795579991453,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/metis/demo"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Ledgerline: EUR 95/month Studio plan, charged to card ending 0617 on the 1st. Invoices stop at 1 Sep 2026 — so no invoice for 1 Oct or 1 Nov 2026. So either subscription cancelled/ended, or billing emails stopped. That''s EUR 95/month = EUR 285 over Sep–Nov that may no longer be charging. Worth flagging: either she cancelled (nothing to worry) or the card 0617 failed and billing lapsed — worth checking.\n\nNow compose answer.\n\nStructure:\n- Headline: Almost nothing lately — last debit alert 25 Sep (two months ago); four small UPI debits in the last six months; nothing since.\n- Table of debits with merchant, ref, balance.\n- Balance trend and the gap: alerts cover only part of the outflow (~INR 7,400 unaccounted between Jun and Sep); and zero alerts in the 61 days since 25 Sep — so email alerts are an incomplete record, they''re not a ledger.\n- Only credit alert in the whole mailbox: 29 Apr INR 6,300, which matches the 17 Apr 6,300 debit (broken lamp purchase + refund).\n- Ledgerline: EUR 95/mo to card 0617; invoice series stops at LL-2025111 on 1 Sep — no Oct or Nov invoice. Either cancelled or lapsed.\n- Phishing warning: two lookalike domains in spam targeting exactly these: konkan-bank-secure.com (15 Sep, \"account suspended\") and ledgerl1ne-invoices.com (9 Sep, \"overdue invoice #88213\"). Real domains: konkanbank.in (alerts@) and ledgerline.io (billing@). Do not act; note the Sep 9/15 dates.\n- Note: no bank/card connection in workspace; this is mail-derived only. Suggest checking account directly for anything after 25 Sep.\n\nKeep concise but complete.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Ledgerline: EUR 95/month Studio plan, charged to card ending 0617 on the 1st. Invoices stop at 1 Sep 2026 — so no invoice for 1 Oct or 1 Nov 2026. So either subscription cancelled/ended, or billing emails stopped. That''s EUR 95/month = EUR 285 over Sep–Nov that may no longer be charging. Worth flagging: either she cancelled (nothing to worry) or the card 0617 failed and billing lapsed — worth checking.\n\nNow compose answer.\n\nStructure:\n- Headline: Almost nothing lately — last debit alert 25 Sep (two months ago); four small UPI debits in the last six months; nothing since.\n- Table of debits with merchant, ref, balance.\n- Balance trend and the gap: alerts cover only part of the outflow (~INR 7,400 unaccounted between Jun and Sep); and zero alerts in the 61 days since 25 Sep — so email alerts are an incomplete record, they''re not a ledger.\n- Only credit alert in the whole mailbox: 29 Apr INR 6,300, which matches the 17 Apr 6,300 debit (broken lamp purchase + refund).\n- Ledgerline: EUR 95/mo to card 0617; invoice series stops at LL-2025111 on 1 Sep — no Oct or Nov invoice. Either cancelled or lapsed.\n- Phishing warning: two lookalike domains in spam targeting exactly these: konkan-bank-secure.com (15 Sep, \"account suspended\") and ledgerl1ne-invoices.com (9 Sep, \"overdue invoice #88213\"). Real domains: konkanbank.in (alerts@) and ledgerline.io (billing@). Do not act; note the Sep 9/15 dates.\n- Note: no bank/card connection in workspace; this is mail-derived only. Suggest checking account directly for anything after 25 Sep.\n\nKeep concise but complete."}],"createdAt":1795580001432},{"type":"text","text":"**Almost nothing — the last money-out alert is 25 September, two months ago, and it was INR 1,250 at a chai shop.** Everything below is from **ana@demo.trymetis.email**; no bank or card is connected to this workspace, so this is mail alerts only, not a ledger.\n\n**Debits on Konkan Bank a/c **4821** (all UPI):\n\n| Date | Amount | Paid to | Reference | Balance after |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Fri 25 Sep 2026 04:10 | INR 1,250 | chaiwala.store@konkan | 427311009876 | 48,210.55 |\n| Sat 12 Sep 2026 06:55 | INR 450 | chaiwala.store@konkan | 427310102947 | 49,460.55 |\n| Sun 2 Aug 2026 20:05 | INR 2,760 | tavola.mumbai@upi | 427310095028 | 52,833.70 |\n| Mon 8 Jun 2026 09:18 | INR 980 | metro.pune@upi | 427310087109 | 60,072.40 |\n\nNothing larger, nothing recurring, nothing unfamiliar. Going back further the same pattern holds — small UPI spends, the biggest a INR 6,300 on 17 Apr which was **refunded in full on 29 Apr** (the only credit alert in the whole mailbox).\n\n**Two things I''d actually look at:**\n\n1. **The alerts aren''t a complete record.** The balance falls faster than the debits explain: 60,072.55 → 52,833.70 between June and August, but only INR 2,760 is accounted for; another ~INR 2,923 disappears between 2 Aug and 12 Sep with just INR 450 documented. So roughly **INR 7,400 of spending since June never generated an alert** — small-ticket UPI below the alert threshold, or auto-debits. And the **61 days of total silence since 25 Sep** is more likely the alerts having stopped than you having spent nothing. Check the account directly rather than trusting the inbox.\n\n2. **Ledgerline looks like it may have lapsed.** The Studio plan is **EUR 95/month, 5 seats, charged to card ending 0617 on the 1st**. Invoices ran monthly for ages — LL-2025106 in April, 107 May, 108 Jun, 109 Jul, 110 Aug, **111 on 1 Sep — and then nothing.** No October invoice, no November invoice. Either you cancelled it, or card 0617 is failing and your Studio subscription is in arrears. Worth confirming before you lose 5 seats of bookkeeping.\n\n**And be careful with two fakes sitting in your spam**, both impersonating these exact senders:\n\n- \"Konkan Bank — Action required: your account **4821 is suspended**\" (15 Sep), from **konkan-bank-secure.com** — real alerts come from **konkanbank.in**.\n- \"Accounts Payable — Overdue invoice #88213, payment required today\" (9 Sep), from **ledgerl1ne-invoices.com** — a numeral **1** for the l, versus the real **ledgerline.io**.\n\nNeither is from your bank or your bookkeeper. Don''t click through or call any number in them; if you want to check a suspension claim, log in directly or call the number on your card.","createdAt":1795580001432}],"metadata":{"modelId":"metis/demo","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Almost nothing — the last money-out alert is 25 September, two months ago, and it was INR 1,250 at a chai shop.** Everything below is from **ana@demo.trymetis.email**; no bank or card is connected to this workspace, so this is mail alerts only, not a ledger.\n\n**Debits on Konkan Bank a/c **4821** (all UPI):\n\n| Date | Amount | Paid to | Reference | Balance after |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Fri 25 Sep 2026 04:10 | INR 1,250 | chaiwala.store@konkan | 427311009876 | 48,210.55 |\n| Sat 12 Sep 2026 06:55 | INR 450 | chaiwala.store@konkan | 427310102947 | 49,460.55 |\n| Sun 2 Aug 2026 20:05 | INR 2,760 | tavola.mumbai@upi | 427310095028 | 52,833.70 |\n| Mon 8 Jun 2026 09:18 | INR 980 | metro.pune@upi | 427310087109 | 60,072.40 |\n\nNothing larger, nothing recurring, nothing unfamiliar. Going back further the same pattern holds — small UPI spends, the biggest a INR 6,300 on 17 Apr which was **refunded in full on 29 Apr** (the only credit alert in the whole mailbox).\n\n**Two things I''d actually look at:**\n\n1. **The alerts aren''t a complete record.** The balance falls faster than the debits explain: 60,072.55 → 52,833.70 between June and August, but only INR 2,760 is accounted for; another ~INR 2,923 disappears between 2 Aug and 12 Sep with just INR 450 documented. So roughly **INR 7,400 of spending since June never generated an alert** — small-ticket UPI below the alert threshold, or auto-debits. And the **61 days of total silence since 25 Sep** is more likely the alerts having stopped than you having spent nothing. Check the account directly rather than trusting the inbox.\n\n2. **Ledgerline looks like it may have lapsed.** The Studio plan is **EUR 95/month, 5 seats, charged to card ending 0617 on the 1st**. Invoices ran monthly for ages — LL-2025106 in April, 107 May, 108 Jun, 109 Jul, 110 Aug, **111 on 1 Sep — and then nothing.** No October invoice, no November invoice. Either you cancelled it, or card 0617 is failing and your Studio subscription is in arrears. Worth confirming before you lose 5 seats of bookkeeping.\n\n**And be careful with two fakes sitting in your spam**, both impersonating these exact senders:\n\n- \"Konkan Bank — Action required: your account **4821 is suspended**\" (15 Sep), from **konkan-bank-secure.com** — real alerts come from **konkanbank.in**.\n- \"Accounts Payable — Overdue invoice #88213, payment required today\" (9 Sep), from **ledgerl1ne-invoices.com** — a numeral **1** for the l, versus the real **ledgerline.io**.\n\nNeither is from your bank or your bookkeeper. Don''t click through or call any number in them; if you want to check a suspension claim, log in directly or call the number on your card."}','assistant','v2','2026-11-25T04:12:47.197Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
