→ 168.\nPage7 (116): 50 → 218.\nPage8 (66): 50 → 268.\nPage9 (16): 15 → 283.\n\nTotal inbox emails: 50*8 + 15 = 415. And all unread ones are the Edge Sender test batch at the bottom (indices 1–265 roughly). Unread count 283.\n\nCheck: unread start at index 283 down to 1 = 283 emails. Indeed the first unread was id 283 (\"html-base64-inline-data-uri-15mb\") and last is id 1. So 283 unread, contiguous block of ids 1–283. Consistent: 415 total, 132 read (ids 284–415).\n\nSo answer: 283 unread, all from \"Edge Sender\"/edge.test synthetic set, dated Jun 2024 back to date-epoch 1970, nothing real; the 132 read include all real mail. Everything unread is older than any real correspondence and is test/deliverability junk — the newest unread is Mon 10 Jun 2024 16:23 UTC.\n\nAlso there''s the spam folder with 8 unread maybe — but question is inbox.\n\nMention \"right now\" as of the turn. Give the breakdown and a note that nothing actionable is unread; the real mail is all read.\n\nI should also mention that unread includes weird items: date-year-9999, 1970 epoch, blank subjects, 100k-char subject, etc. — clearly fixture/test mail.\n\nOffering: label them or archive? I could offer to bulk-label with e.g. custom:clients? no. Maybe offer to mark read — but there''s no mark-read tool loaded; capability exists (\"mark read or unread\") per system prompt. I can offer.\n\nAnswer formatting: short."}],"createdAt":1795580055779},{"type":"text","text":"**283 unread, all of them in the inbox — and every one is junk test mail, nothing real.**\n\nInbox total is **415 messages**: 132 read, 283 unread. All 283 unread form one contiguous block at the bottom, the newest being **Mon 10 Jun 2024 16:23 UTC** — so no unread message is newer than two and a half years old.\n\n**What they are:** a synthetic edge-case batch from `Edge Sender` / `*@edge.test`, evidently a deliverability fixture set rather than anything addressed to you. It breaks down as:\n\n- **201 messages** — `Re: Long thread`, one \"Long thread\" reply per minute from 09:05 to 12:24 on 10 Jun 2024, all in thread `<edge-thread-200-0@edge.test>`\n- **~32 MIME/encoding torture cases** — `enc-invalid-utf8`, `enc-iso-2022-jp`, `mime-boundary-absent`, `enc-rfc2047-broken`, `max-body-plain-20mb`, `mime-nested-100`, a 100k-character folded subject, and similar\n- **~20 attachment cases** — `att-pkpass-zip-bomb`, `att-pdf-2000-pages`, `att-eml-nested-30`, `max-attachments-500`, `att-vcf-1000-contacts`\n- **~18 inline-image and JSON-LD cases** — `img-dimensions-10000x10000`, `jsonld-deep-5000`, `html-base64-inline-data-uri-15mb`\n- **~12 header/date oddities** — `date-year-9999` (dated Fri 31 Dec 9999), `date-epoch` (1 Jan 1970), `date-missing`, `garbage headers`, two blank-subject blank-sender messages, a Unicode/RTL spoof `‮gnp.exe`, and two mutually-referencing `loop A` / `loop B` messages\n\n**Nothing genuine is unread.** Every real thread — Kenji''s Aozora rebrand mail, Raj''s invitations, Priya''s Arabic proofs, the Konkan Bank and Brightloom notifications — is already read. So there''s no \"you have 283 things to deal with\" here, just 283 fixtures inflating the badge.\n\nIf you want the badge cleared, I can bulk-archive the whole `edge.test` block, or mark it read and keep it — say which and I''ll do it. The one caution is that these look like a test corpus someone deliberately loaded into this mailbox, so deleting it might not be yours to do.","createdAt":1795580055779}],"metadata":{"modelId":"metis/demo","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**283 unread, all of them in the inbox — and every one is junk test mail, nothing real.**\n\nInbox total is **415 messages**: 132 read, 283 unread. All 283 unread form one contiguous block at the bottom, the newest being **Mon 10 Jun 2024 16:23 UTC** — so no unread message is newer than two and a half years old.\n\n**What they are:** a synthetic edge-case batch from `Edge Sender` / `*@edge.test`, evidently a deliverability fixture set rather than anything addressed to you. It breaks down as:\n\n- **201 messages** — `Re: Long thread`, one \"Long thread\" reply per minute from 09:05 to 12:24 on 10 Jun 2024, all in thread `<edge-thread-200-0@edge.test>`\n- **~32 MIME/encoding torture cases** — `enc-invalid-utf8`, `enc-iso-2022-jp`, `mime-boundary-absent`, `enc-rfc2047-broken`, `max-body-plain-20mb`, `mime-nested-100`, a 100k-character folded subject, and similar\n- **~20 attachment cases** — `att-pkpass-zip-bomb`, `att-pdf-2000-pages`, `att-eml-nested-30`, `max-attachments-500`, `att-vcf-1000-contacts`\n- **~18 inline-image and JSON-LD cases** — `img-dimensions-10000x10000`, `jsonld-deep-5000`, `html-base64-inline-data-uri-15mb`\n- **~12 header/date oddities** — `date-year-9999` (dated Fri 31 Dec 9999), `date-epoch` (1 Jan 1970), `date-missing`, `garbage headers`, two blank-subject blank-sender messages, a Unicode/RTL spoof `‮gnp.exe`, and two mutually-referencing `loop A` / `loop B` messages\n\n**Nothing genuine is unread.** Every real thread — Kenji''s Aozora rebrand mail, Raj''s invitations, Priya''s Arabic proofs, the Konkan Bank and Brightloom notifications — is already read. So there''s no \"you have 283 things to deal with\" here, just 283 fixtures inflating the badge.\n\nIf you want the badge cleared, I can bulk-archive the whole `edge.test` block, or mark it read and keep it — say which and I''ll do it. The one caution is that these look like a test corpus someone deliberately loaded into this mailbox, so deleting it might not be yours to do."}','assistant','v2','2026-11-25T04:13:40.054Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('c5886496-dcb1-4c05-891e-8985ac0ad961','c2466a74-8c9b-4ece-8e7e-969a549399a5','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"text","text":"<turn sent-at=\"2026-11-25T04:14:15.799Z\" time-zone=\"UTC\" />","createdAt":1795580055809},{"type":"text","text":"Find emails that look like newsletters or digests.","createdAt":1795580055809}]}','user','v2','2026-11-25T04:14:15.837Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('d08335b8-320f-4ab7-a1d5-c675817bf4d2','c2466a74-8c9b-4ece-8e7e-969a549399a5','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The user wants to find emails that look like newsletters or digests. Tools: searchMail; also there''s a label \"newsletter\" built-in. I could search \"newsletter\" and look at sender patterns. Best approach: search mail for typical newsletter/digest signals, and also check which emails carry the `newsletter` label.\n\nCan I search by label? Not directly — searchMail is a query. There''s no \"list emails with label\" tool. Hmm, listEmails folders only. So label-based filtering isn''t available except by searching content.\n\nApproach: run several searches in parallel: \"digest\", \"weekly\", \"newsletter\", \"unsubscribe\", \"this week\", \"month\". Then dedupe and judge.\n\nI already know many candidates:\n- Codeyard \"Your weekly Codeyard digest\" (weekly, several)\n- Kestrel Supply Co. \"This week at Kestrel: ...\" — a retailer''s weekly marketing email (numerous)\n- Paperstack \"Your Paperstack month: ...\" monthly\n- Linkroom marketing (\"Breakout rooms are here\", \"Linkroom for teams: shared recordings\", \"Your Linkroom Pro plan renews...\") — some are product announcements\n- Voltaro Energy bill — not newsletter\n- Ledgerline invoices — no\n- \"This week at Kestrel\", \"15% off this weekend\", \"Spring sale\" — promotional\n\nLet me search to be complete and cite counts. Searches: \"digest\", \"unsubscribe\", \"this week at Kestrel\", \"weekly\", \"month\". Run in parallel.\n\nAlso note: searchMail returns up to some limit (21 results earlier for \"order\"). Might cap. Let''s see.\n\nI''ll run: \"digest\", \"unsubscribe\", \"newsletter\", \"This week at Kestrel\", \"weekly\".","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user wants to find emails that look like newsletters or digests. Tools: searchMail; also there''s a label \"newsletter\" built-in. I could search \"newsletter\" and look at sender patterns. Best approach: search mail for typical newsletter/digest signals, and also check which emails carry the `newsletter` label.\n\nCan I search by label? Not directly — searchMail is a query. There''s no \"list emails with label\" tool. Hmm, listEmails folders only. So label-based filtering isn''t available except by searching content.\n\nApproach: run several searches in parallel: \"digest\", \"weekly\", \"newsletter\", \"unsubscribe\", \"this week\", \"month\". Then dedupe and judge.\n\nI already know many candidates:\n- Codeyard \"Your weekly Codeyard digest\" (weekly, several)\n- Kestrel Supply Co. \"This week at Kestrel: ...\" — a retailer''s weekly marketing email (numerous)\n- Paperstack \"Your Paperstack month: ...\" monthly\n- Linkroom marketing (\"Breakout rooms are here\", \"Linkroom for teams: shared recordings\", \"Your Linkroom Pro plan renews...\") — some are product announcements\n- Voltaro Energy bill — not newsletter\n- Ledgerline invoices — no\n- \"This week at Kestrel\", \"15% off this weekend\", \"Spring sale\" — promotional\n\nLet me search to be complete and cite counts. Searches: \"digest\", \"unsubscribe\", \"this week at Kestrel\", \"weekly\", \"month\". Run in parallel.\n\nAlso note: searchMail returns up to some limit (21 results earlier for \"order\"). Might cap. Let''s see.\n\nI''ll run: \"digest\", \"unsubscribe\", \"newsletter\", \"This week at Kestrel\", \"weekly\"."}],"createdAt":1795580073616},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":11,"emails":[{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","mailbox":"ana@demo.trymetis.email","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM4N10","threadId":"<brz67yl3811n7oj@codeyard.dev>","from":"Codeyard","subject":"Your weekly Codeyard digest","date":"Mon Sep 07 2026 06:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""},{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415