ooms now remember your layout`, `New in Linkroom: live captions in 12 languages` | 4 | Feb 2025 → Sep 2026 |\n| **Northbeam Air** | route/fare marketing — `Fly to Osaka from Frankfurt`, `Summer in Lisbon: city breaks from EUR 79` | 2 | Jun 2025 → Jun 2026 |\n\n**Internal digest (10)** — **Priya Nair**, `[Fernhill Team] Studio weekly, <date>`, 13 Jan 2025 → 14 Sep 2026, every couple of months. Digest-shaped and machine-regular, but written by a colleague, so don''t fold it in with the bulk senders.\n\n**Unsubscribe confirmation (1)** — Tavola, `You''re unsubscribed from Tavola picks`, 7 Mar 2026. The \"Tavola picks\" newsletter itself isn''t in the mailbox; this is just the receipt.\n\n**Three things worth knowing:**\n\n1. **Kestrel is 87% of the noise on its own** — 59 messages. And the 55 \"This week\" issues only ever cycle **eight subjects** (`The candle edit`, `Stoneware from Porto`, `Gifts under EUR 30`, `A kitchen for slow mornings`, `Meet the maker: Oficina Lume`, `Linen, washed and ready`, `Notebooks for the new year`, `Workshop: kintsugi basics`), so it''s the same shop window reopening twice a month for two years.\n2. **The Kestrel series has gone quiet.** 18 Sep → `This week at the shop` on 26 Sep → nothing for two months. Either a list migration or you''ve been dropped/pruned.\n3. **Not everything regular is a newsletter.** I excluded these transactional streams: Konkan Bank alerts and statements, Ledgerline invoices and login codes, Swiftpost tracking, Brightloom order mail, Voltaro Energy bills, Codeyard PR/build/sign-in notices, Linkroom and Paperstack renewal and sign-in mail, Northbeam booking confirmations, calendar invitations.\n\nWant me to label these `newsletter` so the classification sticks? It''s a bulk write across 76 messages and will come to you for approval first — and I''d leave Priya''s `Studio weekly` unlabelled unless you say otherwise.","createdAt":1795580100075}],"metadata":{"modelId":"metis/demo","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"