bd8978c60"},{"fileId":"welcome.txt","name":"welcome.txt","kind":"file","mimeType":null,"size":182,"modifiedAt":"2026-11-25T04:07:51.889Z","driveId":"1ae0b7b1-7ad0-5805-82b9-169bd8978c60"}],"cursor":null},"toolCallId":"call_resp_01a210ea-781b-71c0-9fb0-babb6d1b9cd9_6","toolName":"listFolder","args":{"driveId":"1ae0b7b1-7ad0-5805-82b9-169bd8978c60"}},"updatedAt":1795580151070},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1795580151072,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/metis/demo"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Roots look similar: Team/Finance/Clients/welcome.txt everywhere except the scoped FTP drive (only Clients/), and the two S3 drives have an extra \"edge/\" folder.\n\nBut same names ≠ same files. Need to compare contents. Should I go deeper? The question \"Do all of those drives have the same files in them?\" — a good answer needs content comparison. Let me dig into the subfolders for each drive. That''s 3 folders × 7 drives = ~19 calls. Maybe do Clients, Finance, Team for each of the 7 drives (766b has only Clients). Let''s do it in parallel batches.\n\nLet me list subfolders: for each drive, Clients/, Finance/, Team/ (fileId \"Clients/\" etc.). Let''s issue all in one batch — 4 drives × 3 + ... Let me do drives: 3660 (sftp), d4da (ftp), 766b (ftp scoped, Clients only), 42ff (ftp), cc3f (webdav), b419 (s3), 1ae0 (s3).\n\nBatch: Clients for all 7 = 7 calls; Finance for 6 (all but scoped) = 6; Team for 6 = 6. Total 19 calls in one block. That''s fine but large output. Alternatively, first compare one folder across drives to see if they''re mirrors, then decide. Maybe smarter: list Clients across all 7 first, plus Finance and Team across all — actually just do it all; I need a definitive answer.\n\nAlso could use searchFiles to see everything? searchFiles searches all drives by name/content, but wouldn''t show per-drive differences well.\n\nLet me do the 19 calls. Actually to reduce noise, first do Clients across 7 and Finance across 6 in one batch (13 calls), then Team acros