d real mail → nothing to reply to based on unread. But there might be unanswered threads (last reply from other side). Can''t determine without reading threads; and mail stopped 2 months ago, so likely all settled. I should say: based on unread state, nothing is awaiting reply; if you want, I can check the Aozora thread for anything left open.\n\nStructure:\n- One-line headline: real commitments this week = standups today/Thu/Fri + the Raj 1:1 (already passed yesterday).\n- P1 (today), P2 (this week), P3 (whenever)\nKeep concrete with ids.\n\nTime zone note: all times UTC as per your calendar; standup 09:00 UTC = in ~4h45m.\n\nLet me write, being careful to distinguish real from fixture, and to not overclaim about deleting things (deletion needs approval; and deleting fixtures might not be mine to authorise — it''s an owner decision but the corpus may be needed for testing).\n\nPrioritized list:\n\n**P0 — Today, before 09:00 UTC**\n1. Daily standup 09:00–09:15 UTC, Linkroom room. (Work calendar, recurring Mon–Fri.) Remaining: today, Thu 26, Fri 27.\n2. Prep for the standup using Aozora status? The Aozora work: latest thread Sep 21 \"Rebrand kickoff\", Sep 24 invitation \"Rebrand review Thu Oct 8 15:00\". Those are past.\n\nHmm — those Oct 8 events: \"Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8, 2026 15:00 UTC\" and \"Updated invitation: Aozora logo review (internal) @ Thu Oct 1, 2026 14:00 UTC\" — not in this week''s window and long past.\n\nSo realistic to-do list:\n\nP1 this week (time-boxed):\n- Standup today 09:00, Thu, Fri (real).\n- Decide the fixture purge: 3 places. Fastest wins: mark/archive 283 unread; remove \"Bulk\" + \"Edge cases\" calendars'' fixture events; remove `edge/` from both S3 buckets. All writes need your approval, and the Edge \"Daily forever\" recurrence must be deleted at the series level or it will keep respawning daily.\n- Choose canonical drive (764.../36600459 sftp?) and check drift — because 7 copies will diverge.\n- Restore Finance access question: scoped FTP missing Finance/Team — confirm with... \"Ask Sam for access to Finance/\" but Sam isn''t a member. Note the welcome.txt instruction is stale: no Sam in workspace, and Finance IS visible on 6 drives.\n\nP2:\n- Label newsletters (76) — enables future auto-sorting.\n- Unsubscribe from Kestrel (59 messages, 2 years) — but beware: these may matter to the studio? Kestrel is a *client-adjacent* brand? Kestrel Supply Co. is a shop; the studio does branding for shops. Hmm — Kestrel could be a client''s newsletter, not a subscription. Careful: don''t tell them to unsubscribe from a client. Actually the mailbox gets it at ana@demo... The studio''s clients are Aozora, Kaltwasser, Saffron & Sage. Kestrel isn''t a client. But could be a shop they buy from. I''ll frame as \"decide whether Kestrel is a shop you buy from or a prospect — don''t unsubscribe blindly.\"\n- Mail silence since 26 Sep 2026 — investigate whether intake stopped (2 months with zero real mail is itself a problem). That''s actually a strong P1 candidate: is mail delivery broken? Good insight.\n\nLet me rank:\n1. **Today 09:00 UTC standup** + Thu/Fri.\n2. **Check whether mail intake has stopped** — zero real-mail arrivals since 26 Sep 2026; that''s the anomaly worth 10 minutes.\n3. **Purge the fixture corpus** (decide once, apply in three places) — unblocks badges, week views, drive searches.\n4. **Settle the drive question** — canonical copy + drift.\n5. **Newsletter housekeeping** (label 76, decide Kestrel).\n6. **Fix stale drive guidance** — welcome.txt says \"Ask Sam for access to Finance/\" but no Sam is a member and Finance is already visible on six drives.\n7. Optional: skim Raj 1:1 outcome (it was yesterday 10:00).\n\nGood. Include note that the Raj 1:1 was yesterday — if it was missed, follow up.\n\nWrite concisely with headers and bullets. Include one-line headline."}],"createdAt":1795580307779},{"type":"text","text":"**Two real commitments remain this week — the rest of the \"load\" is fixture data. Here''s the list, most urgent first.**\n\nYour mail has been silent since **26 Sep 2026**, and the week''s calendar holds only standups plus one 1:1 that already happened. So the honest headline: **nothing is genuinely overdue; three cleanups are.** Times are the calendar''s own (UTC).\n\n**1. Daily standup — today 09:00–09:15 UTC** (in under five hours), Linkroom room `linkroom.app/r/standup`. Recurring on the *Work* calendar; also Thu 26 and Fri 27. This is the only live commitment left.\n\n**2. Confirm mail intake hasn''t stopped — 10 minutes, do it today.** The newest message in your inbox is 26 Sep 2026. That''s **two months with zero real mail** — no client thread, no invoice, no bank alert, while Konkan Bank and Ledgerline had been arriving weekly for two years. Either you genuinely went quiet or delivery is broken. Given the letterbox is otherwise healthy-looking, I''d check the provider before assuming quiet.\n\n**3. Decide the fixture purge, then do it once across all three surfaces.** This is one problem wearing three costumes:\n- **Inbox:** 283 unread `edge.test` messages (201 of them a single \"Long thread\") inflating the badge.\n- **Calendar:** a *Bulk* calendar holding ~2 events per four-hour slot all week, plus an *Edge cases* calendar with `Daily forever` and a ten-year all-day event that will bury every week view you ever open. **Delete `Daily forever` at the series level** or it regenerates every day.\n- **Drives:** the `edge/` tree on both S3 buckets (12 folders, `no-content-type.bin`, `one-byte`).\n\nEvery one of those is a write needing your approval, and the corpus may be someone''s deliberate test load — so this is a decision first, then a batch of approvals.\n\n**4. Settle which drive is canonical.** Seven connections hold the same Fernhill tree and **none of them sync**. Pick the one true copy, then I''ll diff the text files (`Meeting notes`, `brand-tokens.json`, `expenses.tsv`, `invoices.csv`) to find what''s already drifted. Until you choose, any edit lands in one of seven places.\n\n**5. Check the Raj 1:1 happened.** *Weekly 1:1 Ana / Raj* sat at **Tue 24 Nov 10:00 UTC — yesterday.** If it slipped, that''s the one follow-up worth sending this week; Raj organises it and it''s the only human-facing meeting on a real calendar.\n\n**6. Newsletter housekeeping — 30 minutes, no deadline.** Label the 76 bulk messages `newsletter` so this classification survives. On **Kestrel Supply Co.** (59 messages over two years, only eight repeating subjects): decide *why* you''re on it before unsubscribing — if they''re a shop you buy from, unsubscribe; if they''re a prospect, route them to a folder instead of cutting the list.\n\n**7. Fix the stale signpost in the drive.** `welcome.txt` on all six copies says *\"Ask Sam for access to `Finance/`\"* — but no Sam is a workspace member (you''re the only member), and `Finance/` is already visible on six of the seven drives. Anyone onboarding from that file will chase a person who doesn''t exist.\n\n**Deliberately not on the list:** replying to mail (nothing unread is real, and every genuine thread is already read), and anything about the scoped FTP drive''s missing `Finance/` and `Team/` — it matches the others inside `Clients/`, so it looks like intentional scoping rather than breakage.\n\nWant me to start with #3? I''d take the calendar first — it''s the change you''ll feel immediately, and the `Daily forever` series is the one thing actively getting worse each day.","createdAt":1795580307779}],"metadata":{"modelId":"metis/demo","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Two real commitments remain this week — the rest of the \"load\" is fixture data. Here''s the list, most urgent first.**\n\nYour mail has been silent since **26 Sep 2026**, and the week''s calendar holds only standups plus one 1:1 that already happened. So the honest headline: **nothing is genuinely overdue; three cleanups are.** Times are the calendar''s own (UTC).\n\n**1. Daily standup — today 09:00–09:15 UTC** (in under five hours), Linkroom room `linkroom.app/r/standup`. Recurring on the *Work* calendar; also Thu 26 and Fri 27. This is the only live commitment left.\n\n**2. Confirm mail intake hasn''t stopped — 10 minutes, do it today.** The newest message in your inbox is 26 Sep 2026. That''s **two months with zero real mail** — no client thread, no invoice, no bank alert, while Konkan Bank and Ledgerline had been arriving weekly for two years. Either you genuinely went quiet or delivery is broken. Given the letterbox is otherwise healthy-looking, I''d check the provider before assuming quiet.\n\n**3. Decide the fixture purge, then do it once across all three surfaces.** This is one problem wearing three costumes:\n- **Inbox:** 283 unread `edge.test` messages (201 of them a single \"Long thread\") inflating the badge.\n- **Calendar:** a *Bulk* calendar holding ~2 events per four-hour slot all week, plus an *Edge cases* calendar with `Daily forever` and a ten-year all-day event that will bury every week view you ever open. **Delete `Daily forever` at the series level** or it regenerates every day.\n- **Drives:** the `edge/` tree on both S3 buckets (12 folders, `no-content-type.bin`, `one-byte`).\n\nEvery one of those is a write needing your approval, and the corpus may be someone''s deliberate test load — so this is a decision first, then a batch of approvals.\n\n**4. Settle which drive is canonical.** Seven connections hold the same Fernhill tree and **none of them sync**. Pick the one true copy, then I''ll diff the text files (`Meeting notes`, `brand-tokens.json`, `expenses.tsv`, `invoices.csv`) to find what''s already drifted. Until you choose, any edit lands in one of seven places.\n\n**5. Check the Raj 1:1 happened.** *Weekly 1:1 Ana / Raj* sat at **Tue 24 Nov 10:00 UTC — yesterday.** If it slipped, that''s the one follow-up worth sending this week; Raj organises it and it''s the only human-facing meeting on a real calendar.\n\n**6. Newsletter housekeeping — 30 minutes, no deadline.** Label the 76 bulk messages `newsletter` so this classification survives. On **Kestrel Supply Co.** (59 messages over two years, only eight repeating subjects): decide *why* you''re on it before unsubscribing — if they''re a shop you buy from, unsubscribe; if they''re a prospect, route them to a folder instead of cutting the list.\n\n**7. Fix the stale signpost in the drive.** `welcome.txt` on all six copies says *\"Ask Sam for access to `Finance/`\"* — but no Sam is a workspace member (you''re the only member), and `Finance/` is already visible on six of the seven drives. Anyone onboarding from that file will chase a person who doesn''t exist.\n\n**Deliberately not on the list:** replying to mail (nothing unread is real, and every genuine thread is already read), and anything about the scoped FTP drive''s missing `Finance/` and `Team/` — it matches the others inside `Clients/`, so it looks like intentional scoping rather than breakage.\n\nWant me to start with #3? I''d take the calendar first — it''s the change you''ll feel immediately, and the `Daily forever` series is the one thing actively getting worse each day."}','assistant','v2','2026-11-25T04:17:55.438Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('392f5456-89ac-4508-bb31-bb33258ba5c8','c2466a74-8c9b-4ece-8e7e-969a549399a5','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"text","text":"<turn sent-at=\"2026-11-25T04:18:27.797Z\" time-zone=\"UTC\" />","createdAt":1795580307812},{"type":"text","text":"Turn that to-do list into a short status update I could paste into chat.","createdAt":1795580307812}]}','user','v2','2026-11-25T04:18:27.849Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('cf77b558-5aa4-43ad-99af-d92011ef0f74','c2466a74-8c9b-4ece-8e7e-969a549399a5','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"User wants a short chat-pasteable status update. Keep it brief, plain, no tool calls needed. Should be prose-ish, drop ids, drop heavy detail. Maybe 120-180 words. Status update voice, first person or neutral? \"Status update\" for chat — likely from Ana''s perspective. I''ll write it as something she can paste, first-person-neutral. Keep it scannable, maybe bullets.\n\nInclude: quiet week, mail silent 2 months (checking), standups, cleanup of test/fixture data across inbox/calendar/drives, drive canonical question, newsletter labeling, nothing overdue.\n\nKeep short. Offer a one-liner version? No, just give it. Maybe note times UTC.\n\nI''ll deliver a pasteable block, and a one-line caveat about what I left out.\n\nDraft:\n\n**Status — week of 24 Nov**\n\nNothing overdue. Real work this week is light: daily standup at 09:00 UTC (today, Thu, Fri) and the Ana/Raj 1:1 ran Tuesday.\n\nThree things in flight:\n- **Mail**: no incoming real mail since 26 Sep. Verifying whether intake has stalled or it''s genuinely quiet.\n- **Cleanup**: a test corpus is sitting in live mail (283 unread), the calendar (Bulk/Edge cases, incl. a daily-forever event) and two drives. Deciding scope, then removing.\n- **Drives**: seven connections hold the same shared-drive tree and don''t sync — picking a canonical one before any edits, then diffing for drift.\n- **Admin**: labelling newsletters; fixing stale \"ask Sam for Finance access\" note in welcome.txt.\n\nNext: standup prep, then cleanup batch.\n\nThat''s decent. Trim word count a bit. Maybe \"nothing overdue\" as opener is good.\n\nKeep ~140 words.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"User wants a short chat-pasteable status update. Keep it brief, plain, no tool calls needed. Should be prose-ish, drop ids, drop heavy detail. Maybe 120-180 words. Status update voice, first person or neutral? \"Status update\" for chat — likely from Ana''s perspective. I''ll write it as something she can paste, first-person-neutral. Keep it scannable, maybe bullets.\n\nInclude: quiet week, mail silent 2 months (checking), standups, cleanup of test/fixture data across inbox/calendar/drives, drive canonical question, newsletter labeling, nothing overdue.\n\nKeep short. Offer a one-liner version? No, just give it. Maybe note times UTC.\n\nI''ll deliver a pasteable block, and a one-line caveat about what I left out.\n\nDraft:\n\n**Status — week of 24 Nov**\n\nNothing overdue. Real work this week is light: daily standup at 09:00 UTC (today, Thu, Fri) and the Ana/Raj 1:1 ran Tuesday.\n\nThree things in flight:\n- **Mail**: no incoming real mail since 26 Sep. Verifying whether intake has stalled or it''s genuinely quiet.\n- **Cleanup**: a test corpus is sitting in live mail (283 unread), the calendar (Bulk/Edge cases, incl. a daily-forever event) and two drives. Deciding scope, then removing.\n- **Drives**: seven connections hold the same shared-drive tree and don''t sync — picking a canonical one before any edits, then diffing for drift.\n- **Admin**: labelling newsletters; fixing stale \"ask Sam for Finance access\" note in welcome.txt.\n\nNext: standup prep, then cleanup batch.\n\nThat''s decent. Trim word count a bit. Maybe \"nothing overdue\" as opener is good.\n\nKeep ~140 words."}],"createdAt":1795580319752},{"type":"text","text":"**Status — week of 24 Nov**\n\nNothing overdue; workload this week is light. Only live commitments are the daily standup at 09:00 UTC (today, Thu, Fri) and the Ana/Raj 1:1, which ran Tuesday.\n\nIn flight:\n- **Mail** — no real incoming mail since 26 Sep. Checking whether intake has stalled or it''s simply quiet.\n- **Cleanup** — test data is sitting in live systems: 283 unread fixture emails, two junk calendars (including a daily-recurring event) and a fixture tree on two drives. Confirming scope, then removing.\n- **Drives** — seven connections hold the same shared-drive tree and none of them sync. Choosing a canonical copy before any edits, then diffing for drift.\n- **Admin** — labelling newsletters to keep the inbox sortable; correcting a stale \"ask Sam for Finance access\" note in the drive''s welcome file.\n\nNext up: standup, then the cleanup batch.\n\n---\n\nTwo notes if you''re pasting this upward: I left out the mailbox address and message counts beyond the unread figure, and the mail-stall item is the only one that could be genuinely bad news — if you''d rather not raise it until you''ve checked the provider, cut that bullet.","createdAt":1795580319752}],"content":"**Status — week of 24 Nov**\n\nNothing overdue; workload this week is light. Only live commitments are the daily standup at 09:00 UTC (today, Thu, Fri) and the Ana/Raj 1:1, which ran Tuesday.\n\nIn flight:\n- **Mail** — no real incoming mail since 26 Sep. Checking whether intake has stalled or it''s simply quiet.\n- **Cleanup** — test data is sitting in live systems: 283 unread fixture emails, two junk calendars (including a daily-recurring event) and a fixture tree on two drives. Confirming scope, then removing.\n- **Drives** — seven connections hold the same shared-drive tree and none of them sync. Choosing a canonical copy before any edits, then diffing for drift.\n- **Admin** — labelling newsletters to keep the inbox sortable; correcting a stale \"ask Sam for Finance access\" note in the drive''s welcome file.\n\nNext up: standup, then the cleanup batch.\n\n---\n\nTwo notes if you''re pasting this upward: I left out the mailbox address and message counts beyond the unread figure, and the mail-stall item is the only one that could be genuinely bad news — if you''d rather not raise it until you''ve checked the provider, cut that bullet.","metadata":{"modelId":"metis/demo","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"}}','assistant','v2','2026-11-25T0